<div class="bb-card">
    <h3 class="bb-card-title"><span class="bb-dot bb-dot-success"></span> &lt;BbScanner&gt; events</h3>
    <div class="bb-scroll">
        <table class="bb-table">
            <thead><tr><th>Event</th><th>Payload</th><th>Raised when</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr><td class="bb-table-key">OnScan</td><td class="bb-mono bb-table-key">BbBarcodeResult</td><td>A symbol is decoded, accepted by <code>AcceptResult</code> and passes duplicate suppression - from the camera, a picked or dropped image, once per symbol.</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="bb-table-key">OnError</td><td class="bb-mono bb-table-key">BbScannerException</td><td>The scanner faults: the camera cannot start or is lost, the options are invalid, or the decoder fails frame after frame. A refused image from the built-in picker is a notice instead.</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="bb-table-key">OnStatusChanged</td><td class="bb-mono bb-table-key">BbScannerStatus</td><td>The lifecycle state changes.</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="bb-table-key">OnCameraChanged</td><td class="bb-mono bb-table-key">BbCameraInfo</td><td>A camera opens, with what was negotiated.</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="bb-table-key">OnDiagnostics</td><td class="bb-mono bb-table-key">BbScanDiagnostics</td><td>At most twice a second, with the last frame's timings. Costs nothing when not subscribed.</td></tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="bb-card">
    <h3 class="bb-card-title"><span class="bb-dot bb-dot-warning"></span> &lt;BbScanner&gt; methods</h3>
    <p class="bb-card-desc">Called through a <code>@@ref</code> to the component.</p>
    <div class="bb-scroll">
        <table class="bb-table">
            <thead><tr><th>Method</th><th>Returns</th><th>Does</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr><td class="bb-table-key">StartAsync(string? deviceId = null)</td><td class="bb-mono bb-table-key">Task</td><td>Opens the camera - the given one, else <code>DeviceId</code>, else by <code>Facing</code> - and starts decoding.</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="bb-table-key">StopAsync()</td><td class="bb-mono bb-table-key">Task</td><td>Stops decoding and releases the camera.</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="bb-table-key">Pause()</td><td class="bb-mono bb-table-key">void</td><td>Stops decoding, keeps the camera open.</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="bb-table-key">Resume()</td><td class="bb-mono bb-table-key">void</td><td>Decodes again after <code>Pause</code>; the symbol in view is reported again unless the window is infinite.</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="bb-table-key">ResetDuplicateFilter()</td><td class="bb-mono bb-table-key">void</td><td>Forgets the values already reported.</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="bb-table-key">GetCamerasAsync()</td><td class="bb-mono bb-table-key">Task&lt;IReadOnlyList&lt;BbCameraDevice&gt;&gt;</td><td>Lists the cameras; labels are generic until permission has been granted once.</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="bb-table-key">GetCameraPermissionAsync()</td><td class="bb-mono bb-table-key">Task&lt;BbCameraPermission&gt;</td><td>What a start would do, without asking the user.</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="bb-table-key">SwitchCameraAsync(string deviceId)</td><td class="bb-mono bb-table-key">Task</td><td>Reopens on another camera without tearing the component down.</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="bb-table-key">SetTorchAsync(bool on)</td><td class="bb-mono bb-table-key">Task&lt;bool&gt;</td><td>Turns the torch on or off; whether the browser accepted it.</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="bb-table-key">SetZoomAsync(double zoom)</td><td class="bb-mono bb-table-key">Task&lt;bool&gt;</td><td>Sets the zoom, clamped to the camera's range; whether the browser accepted it.</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="bb-table-key">OpenFilePickerAsync()</td><td class="bb-mono bb-table-key">Task</td><td>Opens the built-in file picker; results arrive through <code>OnScan</code>. Under Server a call from your own button reaches the page a round trip after the click, which a strict browser may not count as a user gesture; the built-in <em>Scan image</em> button opens the picker in the page itself.</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="bb-table-key">ScanImageAsync(Stream image, int maxSymbols = 16, CancellationToken = default)</td><td class="bb-mono bb-table-key">Task&lt;IReadOnlyList&lt;BbBarcodeResult&gt;&gt;</td><td>Scans an encoded image (PNG, JPEG, WebP...) in the browser; returns the symbols, throws <code>InvalidImage</code>.</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="bb-table-key">ScanImageAsync(ReadOnlyMemory&lt;byte&gt; image, string? contentType = null, int maxSymbols = 16, CancellationToken = default)</td><td class="bb-mono bb-table-key">Task&lt;IReadOnlyList&lt;BbBarcodeResult&gt;&gt;</td><td>The same, from memory; a <code>contentType</code> that is not an image is refused.</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="bb-table-key">ScanCurrentFrameAsync(int maxSymbols = 16)</td><td class="bb-mono bb-table-key">Task&lt;IReadOnlyList&lt;BbBarcodeResult&gt;&gt;</td><td>Reads the camera's current frame at full resolution; throws when the camera is not open.</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="bb-table-key">DecodeImage(ReadOnlySpan&lt;byte&gt; pixels, int width, int height, BbPixelFormat format)</td><td class="bb-mono bb-table-key">BbBarcodeResult?</td><td>Decodes the first symbol in pixels the application has.</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="bb-table-key">DecodeAllInImage(ReadOnlySpan&lt;byte&gt; pixels, int width, int height, BbPixelFormat format, int maxSymbols = 16)</td><td class="bb-mono bb-table-key">IReadOnlyList&lt;BbBarcodeResult&gt;</td><td>Decodes every symbol in those pixels.</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="bb-table-key">DisposeAsync()</td><td class="bb-mono bb-table-key">ValueTask</td><td>Releases the camera and every buffer; Blazor calls it when the component leaves the page.</td></tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </div>
    <p class="bb-card-desc">
        The still image calls - <code>ScanImageAsync</code>, <code>ScanCurrentFrameAsync</code>, <code>DecodeImage</code>
        and <code>DecodeAllInImage</code> - raise no events, search the whole image whatever the <code>Region</code>,
        and use the still image tuning with this scanner's <code>Formats</code> and options.
    </p>
</div>

<div class="bb-card">
    <h3 class="bb-card-title"><span class="bb-dot bb-dot-primary"></span> &lt;BbScanner&gt; properties</h3>
    <div class="bb-scroll">
        <table class="bb-table">
            <thead><tr><th>Property</th><th>Type</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr><td class="bb-table-key">Status</td><td class="bb-mono bb-table-key">BbScannerStatus</td><td>The current lifecycle state.</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="bb-table-key">Camera</td><td class="bb-mono bb-table-key">BbCameraInfo?</td><td>What the browser negotiated for the open camera, or null.</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="bb-table-key">Cameras</td><td class="bb-mono bb-table-key">IReadOnlyList&lt;BbCameraDevice&gt;</td><td>The cameras found by the last enumeration.</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="bb-table-key">Diagnostics</td><td class="bb-mono bb-table-key">BbScanDiagnostics</td><td>Timings of the most recently decoded frame.</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="bb-table-key">FramesDecoded</td><td class="bb-mono bb-table-key">long</td><td>Camera frames decoded since the scanner was created.</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="bb-table-key">FramesWithSymbol</td><td class="bb-mono bb-table-key">long</td><td>Of those, how many held a symbol, before duplicate suppression.</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="bb-table-key">IsTorchOn</td><td class="bb-mono bb-table-key">bool</td><td>Whether the torch is lit.</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="bb-table-key">Zoom</td><td class="bb-mono bb-table-key">double</td><td>The current zoom, or zero without zoom support.</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="bb-table-key">ProcessingSize</td><td class="bb-mono bb-table-key">(int Width, int Height)</td><td>The size frames are decoded at, after <code>MaxProcessingSize</code>.</td></tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </div>
    <p class="bb-card-desc">
        <code>StartAsync</code> is safe to call at any time: a call that arrives while an earlier one
        is still waiting for the permission prompt supersedes it, and the superseded request releases
        its camera rather than leaving it running. The same holds for <code>StopAsync</code> and for
        disposal, so navigating away mid-prompt never leaves the camera indicator lit.
    </p>
</div>

