<div class="bb-card">
    <h3 class="bb-card-title"><span class="bb-dot bb-dot-success"></span> BbScannerOptions</h3>
    <pre class="bb-code">BbBarcodeFormat Formats                    = BbBarcodeFormat.Common
BbScanRegion    Region                     = BbScanRegion.Full
<span class="k">int</span>           MaxScanLines               = 15      <span class="c">// lines per orientation</span>
<span class="k">int</span>           DownsampleFactor           = 1
<span class="k">bool</span>          TryHarder                  = <span class="k">false</span>   <span class="c">// exhaustive detection, full rotation sweep</span>
<span class="k">bool</span>          AllowInverted              = <span class="k">false</span>   <span class="c">// light on dark symbols</span>
<span class="k">bool</span>          TryReversedRows            = <span class="k">true</span>    <span class="c">// linear symbols read right to left</span>
<span class="k">bool</span>          TryVerticalLines           = <span class="k">true</span>    <span class="c">// columns and tilted lines, for rotated symbols</span>
IReadOnlyCollection&lt;<span class="k">int</span>&gt; ItfLengths      = 6..20 even
<span class="k">bool</span>          Code39CheckDigit           = <span class="k">false</span>   <span class="c">// require the modulo 43 check character</span>
<span class="k">bool</span>          Code39ExtendedMode         = <span class="k">false</span>   <span class="c">// interpret Code 39 as full ASCII</span>
<span class="k">bool</span>          CodabarStartStop           = <span class="k">false</span>   <span class="c">// keep Codabar's start and stop letters</span>
<span class="k">bool</span>          RequireEanExtension        = <span class="k">false</span>   <span class="c">// hold EAN/UPC back until its add-on is read</span>
TimeSpan      DuplicateSuppressionWindow = 2 seconds <span class="c">// Zero: every frame; InfiniteTimeSpan: once</span>

BbScannerOptions.ForStillImages()   <span class="c">// 60 scan lines, TryHarder, AllowInverted, no suppression</span>
options.Clone()                   <span class="c">// take a copy before editing a running scanner's options</span>
options.Validate()                <span class="c">// throws on an out of range value</span></pre>
    <p class="bb-card-desc">
        ITF has no check character, so <code>ItfLengths</code> is the main defence against a
        truncated symbol being reported as a shorter, structurally valid number. Narrow it to the
        lengths your application actually uses; an empty collection accepts any even length.
        Give a running scanner a new instance, or a <code>Clone()</code>, rather than editing the one it has:
        a change to <code>Formats</code> or the options rebuilds its decoder without dropping the camera.
    </p>
</div>

<h2>Supporting types</h2>

<div class="bb-card">
    <h3 class="bb-card-title"><span class="bb-dot bb-dot-primary"></span> Regions, points and rectangles</h3>
    <div class="bb-scroll">
        <table class="bb-table">
            <thead><tr><th>Member</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr><td class="bb-table-key">BbScanRegion(double X, double Y, double Width, double Height)</td><td>A part of the frame, each value a fraction from 0 to 1.</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="bb-table-key">BbScanRegion.Full</td><td>The whole frame, the default.</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="bb-table-key">BbScanRegion.CenteredSquare(double fraction)</td><td>A centred square of that fraction of the shorter edge, square in pixels on any camera.</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="bb-table-key">KeepSquare</td><td>Narrows the region to the largest square it holds in a frame's pixels.</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="bb-table-key">IsFull, Normalized(), ForFrame(width, height)</td><td>Whether it covers the frame; clamped into the unit square; as it applies to a frame of that size.</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="bb-table-key">BbScanPoint(float X, float Y)</td><td>A point in frame pixels; <code>Distance(a, b)</code>.</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="bb-table-key">BbScanRect(float X, float Y, float Width, float Height)</td><td>A box in frame pixels; <code>Right</code>, <code>Bottom</code>, <code>Center</code>, <code>FromPoints(points)</code>.</td></tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </div>
</div>

